EGL window surface on an ImageReader, and Transaction.setBuffer onto a SurfaceView

On API 34+ Instagram's photo editor does not draw into its SurfaceView's Surface.
It renders with its own EGL context into an ImageReader (RGBA_8888, the size
surfaceChanged reported) and shows each Image with
SurfaceControl.Transaction.setBuffer(child, image.getHardwareBuffer(), fence,
releaseCallback) on a child of SurfaceView.getSurfaceControl(). Here
EGL14.eglCreateWindowSurface refused the reader's Surface, so the editor opened
with the photo imported and a black preview.

MacApkGlWindow takes an ImageReader as its consumer next to a SurfaceTexture: the
same pbuffer read back at eglSwapBuffers, queued as an Image. ImageReader gains
that producer side (a bounded queue of maxImages, acquireNextImage /
acquireLatestImage, the AOSP "maxImages has already been acquired" exception) and
an Image with one RGBA plane, getHardwareBuffer() carrying the pixels and
getFence(). Bitmap.wrapHardwareBuffer copies such a buffer instead of returning
an empty bitmap. PixelCopy.request(Surface) answers from the reader's last queued
frame.

SurfaceControl records parents (Builder.setParent, Transaction.reparent) and the
SurfaceView a control belongs to; Transaction.setBuffer has the three AOSP
overloads and apply() shows the buffer through the path a lockCanvas frame takes
(SurfaceHolderImpl.macapkPost, split out of unlockCanvasAndPost), then reports
the release from another thread, as a device does. A SurfaceView that receives a
SurfaceControl child answers its holder by the Canvas rule from then on: the
view's own size, shown at the view's rect.

Measured on Instagram 455: the surface is re-announced at 412x412 (it was
412x915, the window), the reader window is created at that size, the first frame
is shown on the per-surface layer at 0,237, and the editor shows the photo. The
1080x1080 image the app renders for upload was inspected and is correct. Still
open: the thumbnail on the "new post" screen stays on its shimmer placeholder.
Cost: one synchronous glReadPixels plus an ARGB conversion per swap.

